Subject: d2d1: custom effects with their own interface pointers, colour contexts

An effect's factory returns IUnknown; Direct2D asks it for
ID2D1EffectImpl, the release used it as one. An implementation with a
separate interface pointer per interface (Paint.NET's) then had
Initialize called through its IUnknown table: its installer died while
it checked the graphics card. CreateColorContext and
CreateColorContextFromDxgiColorSpace return a context instead of
E_NOTIMPL (sRGB, scRGB, or a custom profile kept as given; nothing
converts colours yet). The effect context answers ID2D1EffectContext1
and 2, and hands out its device context, as Paint.NET's effects expect.
tests/samples/d2d1-effect.c checks all of it.
